  <text>
      <body>
         <head>Ballad of Booker T.</head> 
         <lg> 
            <l><persName>Booker T.</persName></l>
            <l>Was a practical man.</l>
            <l>He said, Till the soil</l>
            <l>And learn from the land.</l>
         </lg> 
         <lg> 
            <l>Let down your bucket</l>
            <l>Where you are.</l>
            <l>Your fate is here</l>
            <l>And not afar.</l>
         </lg> 
         <lg> 
            <l>To help yourself</l>
            <l>And your fellow man,</l>
            <l>Train your head,</l>
            <l>Your heart, and your hand.</l>
         </lg>
      </body>
  </text>
